# srv.conf.example - documents every key lib/config.sh understands. This
# file is committed so you can see what's configurable; it's never read
# directly. Your real, per-machine settings live at ops/.state/srv.conf,
# written by `srv setup` (or automatically the first time you run `srv` on
# a box with no srv.conf yet) - .state/ is gitignored, so each machine keeps
# its own values and nothing here syncs between boxes.
#
# Every key is optional. A missing key falls back to a detected default, so
# srv works before you've configured anything - srv.conf only exists to let
# you override what got detected.
#
# Values below are dorm's actual settings, as an example of the shape.

# Where `srv backup` writes snapshots: $BACKUP_ROOT/<app>/<timestamp>/
# Default: /mnt/nas/backups/state if that dir exists, else ~/backups
BACKUP_ROOT=/mnt/nas/backups/state

# Where `srv conf capture` writes redacted configs (the "conf/" half of
# this repo). Default: the repo's own conf/ dir, resolved through symlinks.
CONF_DIR=/home/equa/srv/dorm-config/conf

# Where systemd unit files live.
SYSTEMD_DIR=/etc/systemd/system

# nginx's config root (sites-available/, snippets/, proxy_params live
# under here).
NGINX_DIR=/etc/nginx

# Your home directory - used by srv space's stray-file candidates list.
HOME_DIR=/home/equa

# Mount points `srv live`'s disk section shows. Default: every real
# filesystem findmnt reports (minus /boot and pseudo-filesystems like
# tmpfs). Mark a network mount and it'll be skipped gracefully if it's
# ever unreachable.
WATCH_DISKS=(/ /mnt/nas /mnt/ssd /mnt/videos)

# Detected automatically (apt/pacman/unknown) - recorded for future use,
# nothing branches on it yet.
PKG_MGR=apt

# Root of the local Arch package mirror `srv mirror` manages (only relevant
# if you host one). Default: /mnt/nas/mirror/archlinux if it looks like a
# real mirror (has pool/packages), else unset - "srv mirror" then just says
# "not configured" instead of erroring.
ARCH_MIRROR_ROOT=/mnt/nas/mirror/archlinux

# Where `srv mirror sync` rsyncs FROM. Nothing on a mirror records its own
# origin, so this can't be auto-detected - defaults to a well-known public
# Arch rsync mirror, yours to accept or point at one closer to you.
ARCH_MIRROR_UPSTREAM=rsync://mirrors.kernel.org/archlinux/
